{"parentUuid":"b06236e8-f35b-4894-b5d4-dac5829c65a5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"mcp_instructions_delta","addedNames":["claude.ai Linear","claude.ai Lovable"],"addedBlocks":["## claude.ai Linear\nWhen passing string values to tools, send the content directly without escape sequences. For example, use real newlines in markdown content rather than literal backslash-n (\\n) characters.","## claude.ai Lovable\nLovable is an AI-powered full-stack app builder. The AI agent edits TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui code in a cloud sandbox with a live preview.\n\nNew projects use Lovable's backend default stack. There is no tech stack selector in `create_project`; include framework or rendering preferences in the initial message.\n\nWhat Lovable can build:\n- Landing pages, dashboards, SaaS apps, internal tools, marketplaces, and more\n- Full-stack apps with authentication (Supabase Auth), databases (PostgreSQL), file storage, and edge functions\n- Apps with payments (Stripe), email (Resend), AI features, and 20+ integrations\n- See https://docs.lovable.dev/integrations/introduction for the full integration catalog\n\nHow to interact:\n- Use create_project with initial_message and workspace_id. If multiple workspaces are possible, create_project returns available_workspaces; choose one or ask the user, then call create_project again with workspace_id. After create_project returns projectId, call render_project_widget with that projectId to show build progress.\n- Send natural-language messages via send_message — describe what you want built or changed\n- send_message and create_project initial messages send work from the MCP client's AI agent to Lovable's AI agent on the user's behalf and consume the user's workspace credits.\n- The agent reads your project's code, makes edits, and rebuilds the preview automatically\n- Attach images (designs, screenshots, wireframes) via file uploads to guide visual implementation\n- Use plan_mode=true on send_message to discuss approach before the agent writes code\n- Iterate: review changes with get_diff, then send follow-up messages to refine\n\nEach project has two URLs:\n- editor_url: The Lovable editor where users visually edit their project\n- preview_url: Live preview of the app, rebuilt after each agent response. Share this with users.\n\nKnowledge & skills: Use set_project_knowledge / set_workspace_knowledge for persistent instructions. Use workspace skill tools to create, update, and delete reusable… [truncated]"],"removedNames":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a9a4558e-9247-431b-8b59-f596b5b7c8ac","timestamp":"2026-08-20T16:31:19.302Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"C:\\CentralDark","sessionId":"852e0ea3-325e-4f52-8de9-3367ae94979c","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
